{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289746-martial-arts-houserule","id":1289746,"title":"Martial Arts Houserule","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-19T19:03:32-08:00","id":1289746,"title":"Martial Arts Houserule","content":"I've brought up this rule hack before, but I wanted to discuss it again in light of the Lunar rules.<br /> <br /> I understand the need for the Martial Artist Merit RAW, because of the advantanges built into the Martial Arts Charm rules. Who this screws over however are characters who might want to dabble in one particular style that fits a character concept unrelated to being a martial artist, because it raises the cost of entry on the assumption of taking advantage of the broader rules. So I had a possible fix (that also addresses the Mortal Martial Artist problem, who have literally no advantage to making the point investment in Martial Arts relative to any other combat ability currently)....<br /> <br /> The Martial Artist Merit becomes &quot;Sublime Martial Artist&quot;. With that Merit, the character uses the RAW.<br /> <br /> Without the Sublime Martial Artist Merit...<br /> * characters can still buy Ability dots in Martial Arts styles<br /> * Exalted characters can still buy Charms in those styles they meet the prerequisites for<br /> * Martial Arts Charms from different styles are treated as coming from different abilities and cannot be stacked<br /> * Characters cannot spend [Exalted] XP on Martial Arts Charms<br /> * Dragon-Blooded cannot wield the Immaculate Style Charms without the Merit<br /> <br /> <br /> 1) As i've said this has been discussed a little bit before, but if you have any thoughts on these rules, whether you think they work or not, are balanced, have any tweaks, etc, are welcome!<br /> <br /> 2) Do you think any special rules are needed for limiting Lunars without the Merit? Obviously the most likely possibility is restricting their ability to stack Martial Arts Charms with their Attribute Charms, as that's their main advantage, but I don't know if that'd be too limiting for them and unnecessary with the other limitations of not mixing Charms from different Martial Arts styles, and not being able to spend Lunar XP on Martial Arts Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 02-19-2019, 10:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T19:13:35-08:00","id":1289752,"title":"","content":"Supernal Brawl doesn't extend to MA anyway. You have to pick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T19:25:11-08:00","id":1289756,"title":"","content":"I think your merit's too restrictive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289746-martial-arts-houserule#post1289746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Martial Arts Charms from different styles are treated as coming from different abilities and cannot be stacked</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the only thing you need to worry about for balance's sake.<br /> <br /> In our games, we just make you repurchase the form charm before you can mix it with other martial arts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","name":"Slarn!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T19:26:13-08:00","id":1289757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289746-martial-arts-houserule?p=1289752#post1289752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supernal Brawl doesn't extend to MA anyway. You have to pick.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You are correct. I misremembered thinking of how Brawl being Caste/Favored makes Martial Arts Styles Caste/Favored. I'll adjust.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T19:27:53-08:00","id":1289758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slarn!</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289746-martial-arts-houserule?p=1289756#post1289756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think your merit's too restrictive.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Merit just makes things work RAW. You mean its absence is too restrictive? Because currently not taking the Martial Artist Merit means no Martial Arts at all.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T19:31:37-08:00","id":1289760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289746-martial-arts-houserule?p=1289758#post1289758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Merit just makes things work RAW. You mean its absence is too restrictive? Because currently not taking the Martial Artist Merit means no Martial Arts at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean... you're not playing RAW if you're modifying the rules...<br /> <br /> I just meant that the restrictions on Dragon-blooded from taking Immaculate martial arts or stop people from spending [Exalted] experience on martial arts are unnecessary. You only need to restrict mixing martial arts. That's my take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","name":"Slarn!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T20:32:36-08:00","id":1289776,"title":"","content":"Personally, I don't think we can really judge how dangerous comboing Lunar combat charms and MA is quite yet, so I'd put a pin in that until we have access to more Lunar charms.<br /> <br /> As for me....If someone was building a character and they really wanted this one MA style, I'd probably let them skip the merit on the condition that they could only learn that one style. If they try to go for another style, they need to buy the merit first.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T21:02:08-08:00","id":1289787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289746-martial-arts-houserule?p=1289776#post1289776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I don't think we can really judge how dangerous comboing Lunar combat charms and MA is quite yet, so I'd put a pin in that until we have access to more Lunar charms.<br /> <br /> As for me....If someone was building a character and they really wanted this one MA style, I'd probably let them skip the merit on the condition that they could only learn that one style. If they try to go for another style, they need to buy the merit first.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly don't know what the issue is here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T22:52:53-08:00","id":1289819,"title":"","content":"I've seen Martial Arts Charms in action. At my table, if you want to use Martial Arts Charms, you pay for the Merit.<br /> <br /> Now if you're a Mortal just buying the Abilities, eh, maybe I'll waive the Merit for them. But if they Exalt and want to get the MA Charms then <i>they'll damn well buy the Merit</i>.<br /> <br /> Honestly, for all I see people complaining about how 'expensive' it is... It's really not? It costs the amount as a strong Mutation, or a Demesne, or potentially a very good Daiklave.<br /> <br /> Hell, 5-dot Artifact Weapons are, without Evocations, identical to 3-dot Artifact Weapons and nobody's gone on a row about how they're an unfair tax that I'm aware of, and Evocation trees are often about the same size as a Martial Arts Style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T23:54:02-08:00","id":1289835,"title":"","content":"Artifacts don't cost you creation points/XP just to use any Artifacts at all, and you don't have to buy a new Ability for each Artifact you want to learn Evocations from.<br /> <br /> So there is an extra cost on MA that Artifacts don't have in comparison. If there was a Merit you have to buy for each Artifact you want to unlock the Evocations from before you could access them, I think people would complain about it like they do with the MA Merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T05:37:35-08:00","id":1289875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289746-martial-arts-houserule?p=1289776#post1289776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I don't think we can really judge how dangerous comboing Lunar combat charms and MA is quite yet, so I'd put a pin in that until we have access to more Lunar charms.<br /> <br /> As for me....If someone was building a character and they really wanted this one MA style, I'd probably let them skip the merit on the condition that they could only learn that one style. If they try to go for another style, they need to buy the merit first.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rain the issue I think is trying to be addressed here is less about power and more about stomping on themes people want to do.<br /> <br /> You want to make a Solar who's the most badass Tiger stylist ever? Cool beans.<br /> <br /> Lunars however can combine their native charms with Tiger style. Holes purposefully left in Tiger style can be trivially filled in by native charms. A solar would have to buy up an entire style and do some careful research on what other style to purchase, keeping in mind form weapons and armour. Lunars have an &quot;MA&quot; style that's infinitely expandable, doesn't care what the form weapons are, and doesn't require buying up a whole new ability from 0 -&gt; 5 (If you're a Lunar specialized towards Tiger stylist, your attributes are likely going to reflect this so worrying about prereq's for most charms is largely going to be moot).<br /> <br /> This is before we even touch power, hell this is before we even see the rest of the charms. And oh boy if I'm right then I'm going to have a fun essay to write.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}